                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Surveys in game while playing asking you if you'd recommend it to your friends, bad voice acting and boring gameplay. The bow mechanics are unreliable often shooting way off from  where you're aiming. Also, the positive reviews listed here all have each other on their friendlists and most have only reviewed this game, the reviews may have been manipulated guys watch out.\n\nRefunding this one asap.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1505153154,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1505153154,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 23,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7646077275276184,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "If you played The Lab, the aiming should be the same. But I know that some players have difficulties with it and some don't. You could check some videos like this one https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mnulvo6CasU The most players say once you got it the aiming becomes easy part. From my experience you should go through 10 waves at least. Paradox: when it's getting hot, it's easier to hit the target. \n\nWe always ask the players who loved the game for a public feedback and recommendations to friends. And we appreciate our community members posting reviews. And it's totally normal that not everybody likes the game. So thanks for a review again!",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1505293148,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": true
                    }
